IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 6 Statutory rules and certain other instruments (sections 39 to 45A) and Part 6A Publication of legislation (sections 45B to 45E).
-- The day a statutory rule commences (section 39(1)(b) and (2A)) and the nth sitting day (sections 18, 40(1) and 41(1)) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Sections 44 and 45D are printed "(Repealed)" and have no rule.
-- Facts the Act borrows (which days a House sat, whether a rule is required by law to be approved) are plain inputs.

§ `Part 6 Statutory rules and certain other instruments`

-- Who lays a notice or an instrument before a House. Sections 40(3A) and 45A name two.
DECLARE PersonLayingBeforeAHouse IS ONE OF
    AMinisterLaying
    TheClerkOfTheHouseLaying
    SomeOtherPersonLaying

§§ `39 The making of statutory rules`

-- src:412 | (a) shall be published on the NSW legislation website, and
@ref s 39(1)(a) (src:412)
GIVEN `the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(1)(a) the statutory rule has been published as required` MEANS
    `the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website`

-- src:414 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a statutory rule from specifying different days for the commencement of different portions of the rule.
@ref s 39(2) (src:414)
GIVEN `the statutory rule specifies different days for the commencement of different portions of the rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) prevents the statutory rule from specifying different days for the commencement of different portions of the rule` MEANS
    IF `the statutory rule specifies different days for the commencement of different portions of the rule` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:415 | (2A) Neither the whole nor any part of a statutory rule is invalid merely because (without statutory authority) the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website after the day on which one or more of its provisions is or are expressed to commence. In that case, that or those provisions commence on the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website, instead of on the earlier day.
@ref s 39(2A) (src:415)
GIVEN `the statutory rule is published after the day on which one or more of its provisions is or are expressed to commence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is statutory authority for the publication after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(2A) the whole or a part of the statutory rule is ineffective merely because it is published after the day on which one or more of its provisions is or are expressed to commence` MEANS
    IF `the statutory rule is published after the day on which one or more of its provisions is or are expressed to commence` AND (NOT `there is statutory authority for the publication after that day`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:416 | (3) If an Act provides for the making of a statutory rule by a person or body other than the Governor, but the rule is required by law to be approved or confirmed by the Governor, subsections (1) and (2A) do not apply to the rule unless it has been approved or confirmed as so required.
@ref s 39(3) (src:416)
GIVEN `an Act provides for the making of the statutory rule by a person or body other than the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is required by law to be approved or confirmed by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been approved or confirmed as so required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(3) section 39(1) and (2A) apply to the statutory rule` MEANS
    IF `an Act provides for the making of the statutory rule by a person or body other than the Governor` AND `the rule is required by law to be approved or confirmed by the Governor` AND (NOT `it has been approved or confirmed as so required`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:417 | (4) The Governor may, by order published on the NSW legislation website, exclude any specified class of statutory rules from the application of this section, but may do so only—
-- src:418 | (a) in respect of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act, and
-- src:419 | (b) if, immediately before the commencement of this Act, section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897 did not apply to statutory rules of that class.
@ref s 39(4) (src:417-419)
GIVEN `the class is of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of this Act section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897 did not apply to statutory rules of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exclusion is by order published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(4) the Governor may exclude the class of statutory rules from the application of section 39` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the class is of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act` AND `immediately before the commencement of this Act section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897 did not apply to statutory rules of that class`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the exclusion is by order published on the NSW legislation website` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:420 | (5) This section does not apply to the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 39(5) (src:420)
GIVEN `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(5) section 39 applies to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `40 Notice of statutory rules to be tabled`

-- The time limit for laying the written notice: within 14 sitting days of the House after the day of publication.
-- src:423 | (1) Written notice of the making of a statutory rule must be laid before each House of Parliament within 14 sitting days of that House after the day on which it is published on the NSW legislation website.
@ref s 40(1) (src:423)
GIVEN `days the House sat` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` IS A DATE
      `the day the written notice is laid before the House` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) the written notice is laid before the House within 14 sitting days of the House after the day of publication` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 18 the nth sitting day of a House after a day` `days the House sat` `the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` 14
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (Day `the day the written notice is laid before the House` GREATER THAN Day `the day the statutory rule is published on the NSW legislation website` AND Day `the day the written notice is laid before the House` AT MOST Day last)

-- src:424 | (2) A written notice is to identify the statutory rule to which it relates.
@ref s 40(2) (src:424)
GIVEN `the written notice identifies the statutory rule to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) the written notice complies with the requirement to identify the statutory rule to which it relates` MEANS
    `the written notice identifies the statutory rule to which it relates`

-- src:425 | (3) A written notice shall identify a statutory rule by reference to—
-- src:426 | (a) the Act under which it is made, and
-- src:427 | (b) its citation (if any),
-- src:428 | but need not refer to this Act merely because of the operation of section 26 or 43 in relation to the making of the statutory rule.
@ref s 40(3) (src:425-428)
GIVEN `the written notice refers to the Act under which the rule is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory rule has a citation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written notice refers to the citation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(3) the written notice identifies the statutory rule as the section requires` MEANS
    `the written notice refers to the Act under which the rule is made` AND ((NOT `the statutory rule has a citation`) OR `the written notice refers to the citation`)

-- src:428 | but need not refer to this Act merely because of the operation of section 26 or 43 in relation to the making of the statutory rule.
@ref s 40(3) closing words (src:428)
GIVEN `the only reason for referring to this Act is the operation of section 26 or 43 in relation to the making of the statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3) the written notice must refer to this Act` MEANS
    IF `the only reason for referring to this Act is the operation of section 26 or 43 in relation to the making of the statutory rule` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:429 | (3A) A written notice may be laid before a House of Parliament by a Minister or by the Clerk of that House.
@ref s 40(3A) (src:429)
GIVEN person IS A PersonLayingBeforeAHouse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3A) a written notice may be laid before a House of Parliament by the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN AMinisterLaying THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheClerkOfTheHouseLaying THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherPersonLaying THEN NOTHING

-- src:430 | (4) Failure to lay a written notice before each House of Parliament in accordance with this section does not affect the validity of a statutory rule, but such a notice must nevertheless be laid before each House.
@ref s 40(4) effect on the rule (src:430)
GIVEN `a written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the failure to lay the written notice affects the operation of the statutory rule` MEANS
    IF `a written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:430 | (4) Failure to lay a written notice before each House of Parliament in accordance with this section does not affect the validity of a statutory rule, but such a notice must nevertheless be laid before each House.
@ref s 40(4) the notice must still be laid (src:430)
GIVEN `a written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the written notice must nevertheless be laid before each House` MEANS
    IF `a written notice was not laid before each House of Parliament in accordance with section 40` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:431 | (5) Any provision of an Act that relates to the laying before each House of Parliament of statutory rules made under the Act is of no effect.
@ref s 40(5) (src:431)
GIVEN `it is a provision of an Act that relates to the laying before each House of Parliament of statutory rules made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(5) the provision of the Act has effect` MEANS
    IF `it is a provision of an Act that relates to the laying before each House of Parliament of statutory rules made under the Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:432 | (6) This section does not apply to the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 40(6) (src:432)
GIVEN `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(6) section 40 applies to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `41 Disallowance of statutory rules`

-- Either House may pass a resolution disallowing a statutory rule before the notice is laid, or after it is laid only if notice of the resolution was given within 15 sitting days of the House after the notice was laid.
-- src:435 | (1) Either House of Parliament may pass a resolution disallowing a statutory rule—
-- src:436 | (a) at any time before the relevant written notice is laid before the House, or
-- src:437 | (b) at any time after the relevant written notice is laid before the House, but only if notice of the resolution was given within 15 sitting days of the House after the relevant written notice was so laid.
@ref s 41(1) (src:435-437)
GIVEN `days the House sat` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the relevant written notice was laid before the House` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day notice of the resolution was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) either House may pass a resolution disallowing the statutory rule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the relevant written notice was laid before the House`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST laid THEN
        CONSIDER `s 18 the nth sitting day of a House after a day` `days the House sat` laid 15
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (Day `the day notice of the resolution was given` GREATER THAN Day laid AND Day `the day notice of the resolution was given` AT MOST Day last)

-- src:438 | (2) On the passing of a resolution disallowing a statutory rule, the rule shall cease to have effect.
@ref s 41(2) the rule ceases to have effect (src:438)
GIVEN `a resolution disallowing the statutory rule has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the statutory rule ceases to have effect on the passing of a resolution disallowing it` MEANS
    IF `a resolution disallowing the statutory rule has been passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:438 | (2) On the passing of a resolution disallowing a statutory rule, the rule shall cease to have effect.
@ref s 41(2) the day (src:438)
GIVEN `a resolution disallowing the statutory rule has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 41(2) the day the statutory rule ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF `a resolution disallowing the statutory rule has been passed` THEN JUST `the day the resolution is passed` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:439 | (3) The disallowance of a statutory rule has the same effect as a repeal of the rule.
@ref s 41(3) (src:439)
GIVEN `the statutory rule is disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the disallowance of the statutory rule has the same effect as a repeal of the rule` MEANS
    IF `the statutory rule is disallowed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:440 | (4) If—
-- src:441 | (a) a statutory rule ceases to have effect by virtue of its disallowance, and
-- src:442 | (b) the rule amended or repealed some other Act or statutory rule that was in force immediately before the rule took effect,
-- src:443 | the disallowance of the rule has the effect of restoring or reviving the other Act or statutory rule, as it was immediately before it was amended or repealed, as if the rule had not been made.
@ref s 41(4) (src:440-443)
GIVEN `the statutory rule ceases to have effect by virtue of its disallowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule amended or repealed some other Act or statutory rule that was in force immediately before the rule took effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(4) the disallowance restores or revives the other Act or statutory rule as it was immediately before it was amended or repealed` MEANS
    IF `the statutory rule ceases to have effect by virtue of its disallowance` AND `the rule amended or repealed some other Act or statutory rule that was in force immediately before the rule took effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:444 | (5) The restoration or revival of an Act or statutory rule pursuant to subsection (4) takes effect on the day on which the statutory rule by which it was amended or repealed ceases to have effect.
@ref s 41(5) (src:444)
GIVEN `the other Act or statutory rule is restored or revived under section 41(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the statutory rule by which it was amended or repealed ceases to have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 41(5) the day the restoration or revival takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the other Act or statutory rule is restored or revived under section 41(4)` THEN JUST `the day the statutory rule by which it was amended or repealed ceases to have effect` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:445 | (6) This section applies to a portion of a statutory rule in the same way as it applies to the whole of a statutory rule.
@ref s 41(6) (src:445)
GIVEN `it is a portion of a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(6) section 41 applies to the portion in the same way as it applies to the whole of the statutory rule` MEANS
    IF `it is a portion of a statutory rule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:446 | (7) Any provision of an Act that relates to the disallowance of statutory rules made under the Act is of no effect.
@ref s 41(7) (src:446)
GIVEN `it is a provision of an Act that relates to the disallowance of statutory rules made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(7) the provision of the Act has effect` MEANS
    IF `it is a provision of an Act that relates to the disallowance of statutory rules made under the Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:447 | (8) This section does not apply to the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 41(8) (src:447)
GIVEN `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(8) section 41 applies to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is the Standing Rules and Orders of the Legislative Council and Legislative Assembly` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:448 | (9) This section does not limit any provision of an Act (for example, section 14A (6) of the Constitution Act 1902) that provides that a statutory rule shall not cease to have effect upon its disallowance by either House of Parliament unless it has previously been disallowed by the other House of Parliament.
@ref s 41(9) (src:448)
GIVEN `an Act provides that a statutory rule shall not cease to have effect upon its disallowance by either House of Parliament unless it has previously been disallowed by the other House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has previously been disallowed by the other House` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(9) the statutory rule ceases to have effect upon its disallowance by the House` MEANS
    IF `an Act provides that a statutory rule shall not cease to have effect upon its disallowance by either House of Parliament unless it has previously been disallowed by the other House` AND (NOT `it has previously been disallowed by the other House`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `42 Matters for which statutory rules may make provision`

-- src:451 | (1) If an Act authorises or requires provision to be made for or with respect to any matter by a statutory rule, such a rule may make provision for or with respect to that matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, the provisions of any Act or statutory rule or of any other publication, whether of the same or of a different kind.
@ref s 42(1) (src:451)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires provision to be made for or with respect to the matter by a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1) the statutory rule may make provision for the matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, the provisions of any Act or statutory rule or of any other publication` MEANS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires provision to be made for or with respect to the matter by a statutory rule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- What section 42(2) says a statutory rule may do. The paragraphs and "any combination of those things" are one list.
DECLARE WhatAStatutoryRuleMayDo IS ONE OF
    ApplyGenerallyOrBeLimitedByReferenceToSpecifiedExceptionsOrFactors
    ApplyDifferentlyAccordingToDifferentFactorsOfASpecifiedKind
    AuthoriseAMatterToBeDeterminedAppliedOrRegulatedByASpecifiedPersonOrBody
    AnyCombinationOfThoseThings
    SomethingSection42DoesNotName

-- src:452 | (2) A statutory rule may—
-- src:453 | (a) apply generally or be limited in its application by reference to specified exceptions or factors,
-- src:454 | (b) apply differently according to different factors of a specified kind, or
-- src:455 | (c) authorise any matter or thing to be from time to time determined, applied or regulated by any specified person or body,
-- src:456 | or may do any combination of those things.
@ref s 42(2) (src:452-456)
GIVEN thing IS A WhatAStatutoryRuleMayDo
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2) a statutory rule may do the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN ApplyGenerallyOrBeLimitedByReferenceToSpecifiedExceptionsOrFactors THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ApplyDifferentlyAccordingToDifferentFactorsOfASpecifiedKind THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AuthoriseAMatterToBeDeterminedAppliedOrRegulatedByASpecifiedPersonOrBody THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnyCombinationOfThoseThings THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomethingSection42DoesNotName THEN NOTHING

-- src:457 | (3) This section applies to a statutory rule in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the Act under which the rule is made.
@ref s 42(3) (src:457)
GIVEN `it is a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(3) section 42 applies to the statutory rule in addition to any provision of the Act under which the rule is made` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory rule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:458 | (4) The Governor may, by order published in the Gazette, exclude any specified class of statutory rules from the application of subsection (1) or (2), but may do so only in respect of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 42(4) (src:458)
GIVEN `the class is of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exclusion is by order published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(4) the Governor may exclude the class of statutory rules from the application of section 42(1) or (2)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the class is of statutory rules made under Acts passed before the commencement of this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the exclusion is by order published in the Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `43 Implied power to amend or repeal statutory rules and orders`

-- src:461 | (1) If an Act confers a power on any person or body to make a statutory rule, the power includes power to amend or repeal any statutory rule made in the exercise of that power.
@ref s 43(1) (src:461)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power on a person or body to make a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory rule being amended or repealed was made in the exercise of that power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1) the power to make a statutory rule includes power to amend or repeal the statutory rule` MEANS
    IF `an Act confers a power on a person or body to make a statutory rule` AND `the statutory rule being amended or repealed was made in the exercise of that power`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:462 | (2) If an Act or statutory rule confers a power on any person or body to make an order (whether or not the order must be in writing), the power includes power to amend or repeal any order made in the exercise of that power.
@ref s 43(2) (src:462)
GIVEN `an Act or statutory rule confers a power on a person or body to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order being amended or repealed was made in the exercise of that power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(2) the power to make an order includes power to amend or repeal the order` MEANS
    IF `an Act or statutory rule confers a power on a person or body to make an order` AND `the order being amended or repealed was made in the exercise of that power`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:463 | (3) If the power of a person or body to make a statutory rule or order is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person or body, the power to amend or repeal a statutory rule or order made in the exercise of that power is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of that other person or body.
@ref s 43(3) (src:463)
GIVEN `the power to make the statutory rule or order is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recommendation, approval or consent has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(3) the power to amend or repeal the statutory rule or order is exercisable` MEANS
    IF `the power to make the statutory rule or order is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person or body` AND (NOT `the recommendation, approval or consent has been given`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `45 Presumption of validity of certain instruments`

-- The instruments section 45(2) covers.
DECLARE InstrumentForSection45 IS ONE OF
    AnInstrumentMadeByTheGovernor
    AnInstrumentMadeByAnotherButRequiredByLawToBeApprovedOrConfirmedByTheGovernor
    ARuleOfCourt
    AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentForSection45
    AnotherKindOfInstrumentForSection45

-- src:469 | (2) In this section—
-- src:470 | instrument means—
-- src:471 | (a) an instrument—
-- src:472 | (i) that is made by the Governor, or
-- src:473 | (ii) that is made by a person or body other than the Governor, but is required by law to be approved or confirmed by the Governor, or
-- src:474 | (b) a rule of court, or
-- src:475 | (c) an environmental planning instrument,
-- src:476 | being an instrument or rule of court that is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette.
@ref s 45(2) (src:469-476)
GIVEN kind IS A InstrumentForSection45
      `it is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(2) the thing is an instrument for the purposes of section 45` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeByTheGovernor THEN `it is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette`
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeByAnotherButRequiredByLawToBeApprovedOrConfirmedByTheGovernor THEN `it is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette`
    WHEN ARuleOfCourt THEN `it is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette`
    WHEN AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentForSection45 THEN `it is required by law to be published on the NSW legislation website or in the Gazette`
    WHEN AnotherKindOfInstrumentForSection45 THEN FALSE

-- src:468 | (1) It shall be presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, that all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to the making of an instrument have been complied with and performed.
@ref s 45(1) (src:468)
GIVEN `it is an instrument for the purposes of section 45` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1) it is presumed that all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to the making of the instrument have been complied with and performed` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument for the purposes of section 45` THEN JUST (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) ELSE NOTHING

§§ `45A Tabling of instruments`

-- src:479 | An instrument that, under any other Act, may or must be tabled in a House of Parliament (without any indication as to who is authorised or required to table it) may be laid before the House by a Minister or the Clerk of the House. This section does not affect any other way in which the instrument can be laid before the House.
@ref s 45A (src:479)
GIVEN `under another Act the instrument may or must be tabled in a House of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no indication as to who is authorised or required to table it` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A PersonLayingBeforeAHouse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45A the instrument may be laid before the House by the person` MEANS
    IF `under another Act the instrument may or must be tabled in a House of Parliament` AND `there is no indication as to who is authorised or required to table it`
    THEN CONSIDER person
         WHEN AMinisterLaying THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN TheClerkOfTheHouseLaying THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN SomeOtherPersonLaying THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 6A Publication of legislation`

§§ `45B Definitions`

-- What "legislation" means in Part 6A: three places, and a portion of any of them.
DECLARE LegislationForPart6A IS ONE OF
    AnActOrInstrumentOfThisJurisdiction
    ALawOfAnotherJurisdictionThatAppliesAsALawOfNewSouthWales
    APublicationAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedByReference
    APortionOfAnyOfThose
    SomethingElseNotLegislation

-- src:484 | In this Part—
-- src:485 | legislation means—
-- src:486 | (a) an Act or instrument of this jurisdiction, or
-- src:487 | (b) a law of another jurisdiction that, under such an Act or instrument, applies as a law of New South Wales, or
-- src:488 | (c) a publication applied, adopted or incorporated by such an Act or instrument by way of reference,
-- src:489 | and includes a portion of any such legislation.
@ref s 45B legislation (src:484-489)
GIVEN thing IS A LegislationForPart6A
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45B the thing is legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN AnActOrInstrumentOfThisJurisdiction THEN TRUE
    WHEN ALawOfAnotherJurisdictionThatAppliesAsALawOfNewSouthWales THEN TRUE
    WHEN APublicationAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedByReference THEN TRUE
    WHEN APortionOfAnyOfThose THEN TRUE
    WHEN SomethingElseNotLegislation THEN FALSE

§§ `45C Publication on NSW legislation website`

-- What the Parliamentary Counsel may publish under section 45C(1).
DECLARE MatterThatMayBePublished IS ONE OF
    LegislationAsOriginallyMadeOrAsAmended
    TheGazetteAsIndividualNoticesOrAsACollection
    OtherMatterIncludingInformationRelatingToLegislation

-- src:492 | (1) The Parliamentary Counsel may publish on the NSW legislation website under the authority of the Government—
-- src:493 | (a) legislation (as originally made or as amended), and
-- src:494 | (a1) the Gazette (as individual gazette notices or as a collection of gazette notices), and
-- src:495 | (b) other matter (including information relating to legislation and any matter authorised by law to be published on the website).
@ref s 45C(1) (src:492-495)
GIVEN matter IS A MatterThatMayBePublished
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45C(1) the Parliamentary Counsel may publish the matter on the NSW legislation website under the authority of the Government` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN LegislationAsOriginallyMadeOrAsAmended THEN TRUE
    WHEN TheGazetteAsIndividualNoticesOrAsACollection THEN TRUE
    WHEN OtherMatterIncludingInformationRelatingToLegislation THEN TRUE

-- src:496 | (2) Legislation, the Gazette or other matter is published on the NSW legislation website—
-- src:497 | (a) if it is made accessible in full on that website, or
-- src:498 | (b) if notice of its making, issue or other production is made accessible on that website and it is made accessible separately in full on that website or in any other identified location.
@ref s 45C(2) (src:496-498)
GIVEN `it is made accessible in full on that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of its making, issue or other production is made accessible on that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made accessible separately in full on that website or in any other identified location` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45C(2) the legislation, the Gazette or other matter is published on the NSW legislation website` MEANS
    IF `it is made accessible in full on that website` OR (`notice of its making, issue or other production is made accessible on that website` AND `it is made accessible separately in full on that website or in any other identified location`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:499 | (3) The date on which legislation, the Gazette or other matter is published on the NSW legislation website is the date notified by the Parliamentary Counsel as the date of its publication (being not earlier than the date on which it was first made so accessible).
@ref s 45C(3) (src:499)
GIVEN `the date notified by the Parliamentary Counsel as the date of publication` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it was first made so accessible` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 45C(3) the date on which the legislation, the Gazette or other matter is published on the NSW legislation website` MEANS
    IF Day `the date notified by the Parliamentary Counsel as the date of publication` AT LEAST Day `the date on which it was first made so accessible`
    THEN JUST `the date notified by the Parliamentary Counsel as the date of publication`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:500 | (4) If legislation, the Gazette or other matter cannot for technical or other reasons be published on the NSW legislation website at a particular time, the legislation, the Gazette or other matter may be published at that time in such other manner as the Parliamentary Counsel determines and published on that website as soon as practicable thereafter. In that case, it is taken to have been published on that website at that earlier time.
@ref s 45C(4) (src:500)
GIVEN `it cannot for technical or other reasons be published on the NSW legislation website at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published at that time in such other manner as the Parliamentary Counsel determines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published on that website as soon as practicable thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45C(4) the legislation, the Gazette or other matter is taken to have been published on that website at that earlier time` MEANS
    IF `it cannot for technical or other reasons be published on the NSW legislation website at a particular time` AND `it is published at that time in such other manner as the Parliamentary Counsel determines` AND `it is published on that website as soon as practicable thereafter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:501 | (5) The Parliamentary Counsel is to compile and maintain a database of legislation or Gazettes published on the NSW legislation website, and may certify the form of legislation or Gazettes so published that is correct.
@ref s 45C(5) (src:501)
GIVEN `it is legislation or a Gazette published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45C(5) the Parliamentary Counsel is to compile and maintain a database of it and may certify the form of it that is correct` MEANS
    IF `it is legislation or a Gazette published on the NSW legislation website` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- What the Parliamentary Counsel may determine under section 45C(6).
DECLARE MatterThePCMayDetermine IS ONE OF
    TheRequirementsForLodgingInstrumentsRequiredToBePublished
    StandardTechnicalRequirementsForTheDraftingOrFormOfThoseInstruments
    SomeOtherMatterNotNamedInSection45C6

-- src:502 | (6) For the purpose of facilitating public access to instruments on the NSW legislation website, the Parliamentary Counsel may determine the following matters—
-- src:503 | (a) the requirements for lodging instruments required to be published on that website,
-- src:504 | (b) standard technical requirements with respect to the drafting or form of those instruments.
@ref s 45C(6) (src:502-504)
GIVEN matter IS A MatterThePCMayDetermine
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45C(6) the Parliamentary Counsel may determine the matter for the purpose of facilitating public access to instruments on the NSW legislation website` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN TheRequirementsForLodgingInstrumentsRequiredToBePublished THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN StandardTechnicalRequirementsForTheDraftingOrFormOfThoseInstruments THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherMatterNotNamedInSection45C6 THEN NOTHING

§§ `45E Style changes, roman numerals, colons and dashes`

-- The changes section 45E(1) allows when legislation is published.
DECLARE ChangeInPublishing IS ONE OF
    OmissionOfTheEnactingFormula
    OmissionOfACommaBeforeOrAfterTheYearInTheCitation
    OmissionOfInvertedCommasAroundTheCitation
    OtherChangeToTheFormatToConformToCurrentStyles
    AChangeToTheTextOfTheLegislation

-- src:510 | (1) Legislation may be published under this Part—
-- src:511 | (a) with the omission of the enacting formula, and
-- src:512 | (b) with the omission of any comma before or after the year in the short title or citation of the legislation (or in references to the short title or citation of legislation of this or any other jurisdiction), and
-- src:513 | (c) with the omission of inverted commas around the short title or citation of legislation, and
-- src:514 | (d) with other changes to the format (but not to the text) of legislation so as to conform to current styles in the State.
@ref s 45E(1) (src:510-514)
GIVEN change IS A ChangeInPublishing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45E(1) legislation may be published under Part 6A with the change` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN OmissionOfTheEnactingFormula THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN OmissionOfACommaBeforeOrAfterTheYearInTheCitation THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN OmissionOfInvertedCommasAroundTheCitation THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN OtherChangeToTheFormatToConformToCurrentStyles THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AChangeToTheTextOfTheLegislation THEN JUST FALSE

-- The pairs section 45E(2) says may be regarded as interchangeable.
DECLARE PairOfSymbols IS ONE OF
    RomanNumeralsAndTheCorrespondingArabicNumerals
    ColonsAndDashes
    SomeOtherPairOfSymbols

-- src:515 | (2) For the purposes of publication under this Part and for all other purposes—
-- src:516 | (a) roman numerals in legislation may be regarded as being interchangeable with the corresponding arabic numerals, and
-- src:517 | (b) colons in legislation may be regarded as being interchangeable with dashes.
@ref s 45E(2) (src:515-517)
GIVEN pair IS A PairOfSymbols
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45E(2) the pair may be regarded as interchangeable in legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER pair
    WHEN RomanNumeralsAndTheCorrespondingArabicNumerals THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ColonsAndDashes THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherPairOfSymbols THEN NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Parts 6 and 6A`

-- A sample of the days a House sat: 3 to 18 March 2026, sixteen days in a row (the sample stands in for the borrowed fact, which the Act does not state).
`sample days the House sat` MEANS LIST (Date 3 3 2026), (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 6 3 2026), (Date 7 3 2026), (Date 8 3 2026), (Date 9 3 2026), (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026), (Date 12 3 2026), (Date 13 3 2026), (Date 14 3 2026), (Date 15 3 2026), (Date 16 3 2026), (Date 17 3 2026), (Date 18 3 2026)

